      "id": 4,
      "claim": "The other options (stream water, garden rock, beach waves) primarily involve the transport or slow mechanical breakdown of existing material rather than the rapid generation of new organic soil.",
      "evidence": "Fluvial and coastal processes are erosional/transport mechanisms; rock weathering is extremely slow (mm/kyr); none of these generate the organic humus component as quickly as biological decay.",
      "weight": 0.2,
      "depends_on": [1]
    },
