      "claim": "Despite the technical nuance, the rotting log is still the fastest process to contribute to the formation of a new, distinct soil layer because it introduces the critical organic component that defines topsoil, whereas the other options do not create new soil material at all.",
      "evidence": "Without organic matter, the material is just weathered rock or sediment. The log's decomposition transforms raw organic material into humus, which is the defining characteristic of new soil formation in a biological context.",
